Q: I have spondylosis and osteoporosis and my doctor requires me to take collagen as part of treatment. But I have been a vegetarian for 14 years. Can I take normal collagen?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general,introduction
  ✓ substantial reply (>600 chars)
  ✓ ends cleanly (punctuation/emoji, not mid-word)
  ✓ answers the vegetarian-collagen question
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
This is a really thoughtful question, and it shows how sincerely you're trying to honour both your health and your vows 🙏

---

**Master Lu's teaching on this:**

Most collagen supplements are derived from animal sources (fish, bovine, porcine). Since you have made a vegetarian vow, this is something to consider carefully.

From the retrieved teachings, Master Lu addressed a similar situation — when vegetarians need to consume medicine or health supplements containing animal by-products like gelatine or fish oil:

> When you consume any medicine or health supplements that contain ingredients such as gelatine or fish oil, if your body does not reject the taste, then perhaps you have not reached the level where you are completely observing your precepts. However, it would still be best to avoid consuming such products as they contain animal by-products.

— *Buddhism Q&A (EN)*

---

**Practical guidance based on Master Lu's teachings:**

**Option 1: Seek plant-based alternatives first**

Master Lu consistently encouraged vegetarians to find alternative nutrition sources. He taught:

> Vegetarian food can be very healthy and nutritious... You can also take health supplements including soy lecithin and calcium if necessary.

— *Buddhism Q&A (EN)*

For collagen support specifically, you may want to discuss with your doctor whether **plant-based collagen boosters** (which contain Vitamin C, amino acids, and antioxidants that help your body produce its own collagen) could be a suitable alternative.

**Option 2: If your doctor says there is truly no alternative**

Master Lu's teaching shows compassion for genuine medical necessity. If you have truly exhausted plant-based options and your doctor insists that animal-derived collagen is medically necessary, you can sincerely inform Guan Yin Bodhisattva:

*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva forgive me, [your full name]. I am taking this for medical treatment because I have no choice. I do not wish to break my vegetarian vow."*

Then recite the **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance** sincerely to repent.

**The key principle Master Lu emphasised:**

> Most importantly, it is all about your intention.

— *Buddhism Q&A (EN)*

If you take it purely for medical necessity with a sincere and reluctant heart — that is very different from enjoying or seeking it out.

---

**My suggestion:**

1. First consult your doctor about **plant-based collagen alternatives**
2. If truly no alternative exists, inform Bodhisattva sincerely before taking
3. Continue your recitations diligently — your 14 years of vegetarianism is a tremendous merit 🙏
4. Recite the **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance** to repent if you do need to take animal collagen

Guan Yin Bodhisattva sees your sincere heart. You have kept your vow for 14 years — that itself is a great offering 🙏

