--- reply ---
That's a real and heavy feeling — when work keeps going wrong, it's hard not to wonder *why*. 🙏

The short answer from Master Lu's teachings: **yes, our life circumstances — including career — are connected to karma**. But the more important question is: what can we do about it?

Master Lu teaches us that karma isn't a life sentence. It can be changed through sincere practice.

---

**What might be contributing to career difficulties:**

From Master Lu's perspective, career obstacles often involve one or more of these:

- **Karmic creditors** (冤亲债主) — people or beings we've harmed in past or present lives, who now create obstruction in our lives
- **Karmic obstacles** (业障) — accumulated from wrongdoings in this life or past lives
- **Insufficient merit** — not enough good deeds to support the career we want

---

**What you can do — starting today:**

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒)** — 3 to 7 times daily
*Before reciting, say:* "Please Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me [your full name] with good health and strength"

📿 **Heart Sutra (心经)** — 3 to 7 times daily
*Before reciting, say:* "Please Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me [your full name] with wisdom and clarity of mind, and remove my worries"
⚠️ Do not recite after 10pm

📿 **Cundi Mantra (准提神咒)** — 21 times daily
*Before reciting, say:* "Please Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me [your full name] with success in my career and that things go smoothly"

📿 **Disaster-Eliminating Auspicious Mantra (消灾吉祥神咒)** — 21 to 49 times daily
*Before reciting, say:* "Please Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me [your full name] with the elimination of disasters and auspiciousness"

---

**One more thing — making a vow**

Master Lu teaches that making a sincere vow in front of Guan Yin Bodhisattva can accelerate change. A simple vow like: *"I vow to eat vegetarian on the 1st and 15th of each lunar month"* or *"I vow to release living beings"* — done sincerely — can open doors.

---

If you haven't started reciting regularly yet, the best first step is simply:

🔗 Follow along with this teaching video: [https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/](https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/)

Have you been reciting before, or is this new for you? 🙏

═══ CHIP4-en My child is rebell — guard: passed_after_retry ═══
Q: My child is rebellious, how should I handle my emotions?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
This is such a tender kind of pain — loving your child deeply, and yet feeling like there's a wall between you. 🙏

Master Lu's teachings give us a very clear and compassionate way to understand this situation.

From the retrieved teachings in *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3*:

> First of all, you should not use the analytical mind of adults to interpret the naive and playful nature of children.

This is such an important reminder — sometimes what we see as "rebellion" is actually a child's nature expressing itself in ways we don't yet understand.

Master Lu also teaches that if a child is in conflict with parents or family members, it may be due to **negative karmic ties from previous lives**, or the child may have come into the parents' lives to collect karmic debts. This is not to blame anyone — it's simply the nature of karma playing out.

---

### For your own emotions right now:

The most important thing is to **stabilise your own heart first**. When we are in emotional pain, we cannot guide our children well.

Try these:

📿 **Heart Sutra** — at least 7 times daily  
Prayer: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], to open my wisdom, have a calm and clear mind, and remove my worries."*  
*(Avoid reciting after 10pm)*

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 to 7 times daily  
Prayer: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], with good health and increased spiritual strength."*

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots** — 21 times daily  
Prayer: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], and [child's full name] to resolve our karmic conflicts."*

---

### For your child:

You can also recite on your child's behalf:

- **Heart Sutra** — the more the better — to help your child gain wisdom and be more cooperative
- **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 to 7 times daily for the child (if the child is stubborn or misbehaving, keep it to 7 times — reciting too many times may increase the child's spiritual energy and make them harder to discipline)

---

The key teaching from Master Lu is this: **lead by example, not by force**. When you yourself become calmer, more patient, and more spiritually grounded through recitation, children often naturally begin to shift.

Keep going steadily. Guan Yin Bodhisattva is watching over your family. 🙏

Have you been reciting regularly, or is this relatively new to you?

